+### 4.1b COLLISION MAP — compare only where upstream crossed OUR changes (President law 2026-08-29)
+
+Two duties on EVERY bump/ingest, and the second is scoped tightly on his order:
+
+1. **Nothing of OURS is lost.** The series replay (4.1) proves each patch still applies; a patch
+   dropped, skipped, or emptied by the rebase is a STOP, never a footnote.
+2. **A/B only at INTERSECTIONS.** Compute the collision map:
+   `git diff --name-only <old-base>..<new-base>` ∩ the files the series touches
+   (`git diff --name-only <new-base>..arifi/main`). For every intersecting file, look at whether the
+   upstream delta touches the SAME functions/hunks as our patches:
+   - Upstream unchanged at our change-points → **no comparison owed** (identical-to-pre-our-change
+     is not a signal; do not burn a bench on it).
+   - Upstream moved code we also changed → **named collision**: record it in the bump report and run
+     the targeted before/after (perf and/or quality, from OUR baseline) for that surface only.
+   The collision list, empty or not, is a REQUIRED line in the bump report — "no intersections" is
+   a checked claim, not an assumption.
+
